{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/storypath-system/1503888-storypath-combat-target-outnumbered","id":1503888,"title":"[Storypath] Combat - Target outnumbered","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion","Storypath System"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-25T05:54:56-08:00","id":1503888,"title":"[Storypath] Combat - Target outnumbered","content":"In Scion 2E some powers are mentioning combat character being outnumbered - but I cannot find particular rules in books. Someone maybe know what they are?<br /> <br /> I vaguely remember that maybe Defense of target is lowered by 1 for each attacker after first in the turn? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Power from <b>Scion</b> mentioning being outnumbered<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'Scion Hero p. 236' </strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Army of One:</b> When you fight outnumbered, you do not take any penalties or increased difficulty that being outnumbered would cause. You gain half your Legend, round up as an Enhancement to all attacks so long as there are more opponents present than you and your band. When fighting a greater force as a Feat of Scale, invoke your Legendary Title and imbue Legend instead of spending it.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}